# What is the air you breathe made of?
subtitle: "Share out the pie: how much of the air you breathe is nitrogen, oxygen and argon? Then see where carbon dioxide's tiny sliver fits."

## What is the air you breathe made of?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
use: pie_chart
with:
    labels:
      - Oxygen
      - Argon & rest
      - Nitrogen
    values:
      - 20.95
      - 0.97
      - 78.08
sources:
    - id: noaa
      title: Trends in atmospheric carbon dioxide
      authors: NOAA Global Monitoring Laboratory
      year: 2025
      url: https://gml.noaa.gov/ccgg/trends/
      finding: CO2 is about 420-425 ppm (about 0.04 %), up from about 280 ppm before 1750
    - id: comp
      title: Atmosphere of Earth
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atmosphere_of_Earth
      finding: dry air is 78.08 % nitrogen, 20.95 % oxygen, 0.93 % argon, about 0.04 % carbon dioxide

    circle breath "air" #2f6b8f x 500 y 420 width 380 font_size 72 hidden true
    text rise "+50 % since 1750" #b5482e cites ["noaa"] x 832 y 262 font_size 28 hidden true
    text lazy "argos = lazy" #8f6aa8 x 862 y 402 font_size 30 hidden true
    text co2 "CO₂: 0.04 %" #b5482e cites ["noaa"] x 832 y 322 font_size 36 hidden true
    path co2_hair dashed #b5482e points [[758,330],[752,446]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true

    card title "What is air made of?"

Take a breath. What is that air actually made of?
    draw breath

    hide breath

    ask "How is the air split? Drag the dividers to share out the pie." on all store g default 55,5,40
        right: Close on all three.
        wrong: Not quite. One gas hogs almost the whole pie.

Nitrogen is the giant: seventy-eight percent of every breath.
    highlight slice_3

And it goes straight back out again: our bodies can't use it at all.
    text inout "in → out" #8f6aa8 x 190 y 330 font_size 34

Oxygen, the gas we actually need, is only about a fifth.
    highlight slice_1

Nearly all the rest is argon, a gas so unreactive that its name comes from the Greek for lazy.
    draw lazy

And carbon dioxide, the gas behind global warming?
    draw co2 co2_hair

About 0.04 percent: four molecules in every ten thousand.
    highlight co2

Tiny, yet that share has grown by half since before the industrial age.
    draw rise

